 "text": "Hello there! How's your day treating you? It depends on how much it looks like new versus how many miles are actually on it. Stick a finger under the valve and pump until the hiss stops, then a few more times. Then fill the tire and pump until the valve doesn't move. Pump it up and let it air down a bit, then pump it back up. Whichever tire feels low without having to be pumped for real, that's the one. Then inflate both to the same pressure and ride them for a week or so to catch any slow leaks.",
